Epi Info 3.5.4 tutorial project files (EIHAT)
=============================================

The files under this directory are verbatim, unmodified copies of the sample
datasets and project files distributed by the CDC for the Epi Info™ Community
Health Assessment Tutorial (Epi Info 3.5.4):

    Archive    : EIHATProjectFiles.zip ("EIHAT Project Files" folder)
    URL        : https://www.cdc.gov/epiinfo/zipfiles/eihat/EIHATProjectFiles.zip
    Page       : https://www.cdc.gov/epiinfo/support/downloads/eihat.html
                 (mirrored at https://restoredcdc.org/www.cdc.gov/epiinfo/support/downloads/eihat.html)
    SHA-256    : 9954794cc6d721c6c50030f284e7f3d0a4f53cbacee8cff0667a039b37a17dee (the ZIP)
    Publisher  : U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, Centers for
                 Disease Control and Prevention, National Center for Public
                 Health Informatics (tutorial document version 2.0,
                 October 2005)

Licence (decision D12 — verdict: redistributable, pending OWNER REVIEW):

    The companion tutorial document (EIHATFull.pdf, "Copyright Information")
    states: "Epi Info is a trademark of CDC. Epi Info™ programs are provided
    in the public domain to promote public health. Programs may be freely
    translated, copied, or distributed. No warranty is made or implied for
    use of the software for any particular purpose."

    The tutorial and its project files are a U.S. government work product
    published by HHS/CDC; the ZIP itself contains no licence file. The
    document notes production "by the collaborative efforts of the Centers
    for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), the Assessment Initiative (AI),
    and the New York State Department of Health (NYSDOH)" and that it "has
    been designed using asthma data provided to the CDC by the NYSDOH" — the
    analysis data are synthetic sample data created for the tutorial. This
    NYSDOH-collaboration caveat is recorded in docs/decisions.md under
    "v1.1 Task 2 — legacy samples (D12)" for the owner's review.

Omitted from this copy: `censusage_files/` — saved-web-page assets (CDC site
CSS/JS/GIF chrome) accompanying `censusage.htm`; they are page scaffolding,
not tutorial data, and are not needed by later tasks. Every other file in the
archive is present and unmodified; SHA-256 of every file is recorded in
../SHA256SUMS. "Epi Info" is a trademark of the CDC and is used descriptively
only.
